CONTROLS
  [PASS] C1 counts: S1 nine; ALPAKA ten discs at z >= 2 of which nine carry M*; CRISTAL groups 12 / 6 / 6 / 6; S4 the RC100 corrected rows at z >= 2 (reported): S1 9; ALPAKA 10 / 9; CRISTAL [12, 6, 6, 6]; S4 41
  [PASS] C2 non-vacuous placement: S1 galaxies with g_obs set exactly on each law through V and r give delta_L = 0 under their own law and |delta| > 1e-3 under the other laws in >= 90% of the rows: max |delta| 9.6e-17; other-law sensitivity 100%
  [FAIL] C3 the disc function: Freeman's peak V^2 = 0.3872 G M / R_d to 0.003 and V^2 -> G M / r far away (r = 50 R_d) to 1e-3: peak 0.3870; far field ratio 1.00181
  [PASS] C4 band direction: raising the gas mass raises g_bar and lowers every delta_L at every S1 point (tau = +0.3 < 0 < -0.3): True
  [PASS] C5 the CRISTAL group medians of delta_FLAT and delta_H(z) equal CFG222's committed values to 1e-9 and the RC100 corrected loader reproduces CFG216's committed FLAT slope: CRISTAL max |difference| 8.3e-17; RC100 slope difference 0.0e+00

4/5 controls pass; 0 s
Reading rule: compilation; conversions as published; calibration-limited; the S1 / S3 baryon models are ours (thin exponential discs, the tabulated R_e for stars and gas); ALPAKA points are stars-only lower limits on g_bar; LambdaCDM has no a0; no sentence says the data favour a law.
